On a second, unrelated note, I had issue running the correlate residuals function (beginning of 4.6 in your manual) because an error was showing for N not being an object. I realized that I had failed to include the "N <- which(abs(densities - 0.10) < 0.001)" line when initializing my variables. However, I did not run this initially because it says that this is for when you are interested in a specific density, but I thought that the densities where sequentially set in the init.vars function? What is the importance of N in the pipeline and how best should it be used/set?

